# Pairs with OnlySupersededRefused. The floor check is put back into the append
# steps' guards, leaving the admission predicate alone, so a property defined
# through that predicate would not see it. The behavioural property does: a live
# leaf's append is refused after another leaf's retirement (#5635).
MODULE: OnlySupersededRefusedFloorInAppendGuards
TARGET: OnlySupersededRefused
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the append guards check the partition's retired floor beside the entry
PERTURBS: OwnAlloc, StaleAppend

--- FIND
    /\ AppendAdmits(a)
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the floor is checked in the guard.
    /\ AppendAdmits(a) /\ epoch[a] > retired
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ ~AppendAdmits(a)
    /\ up' = up \ {a}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the floor is checked in the guard.
    /\ ~AppendAdmits(a) \/ epoch[a] <= retired
    /\ up' = up \ {a}
--- END
